    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0527" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">554.A2/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Italian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                            Martino</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to your note of August 2,
                    1927, inviting the Government of the United States to participate in the
                    International Conference on Copyright to open at Rome on May 8 next,<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d303-f1"/> I have the honor now to inform you that, after
                    reconsideration, it has been decided to accept the invitation and that the
                    Honorable Henry P. Fletcher, American Ambassador at Rome, Mr. Thorvald Soltterg,
                    Register of Copyrights, Library of Congress, and the Honorable Sol Bloom, Member
                    of Congress, have been designated to attend the Congress as delegates on the
                    part of the United States. <pb facs="0528" n="400" xml:id="pg400"/> The American
                    Ambassador at Rome was instructed by cable on April 25<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d303-f2"/> to advise your Government accordingly.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank B. Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d303-f1" n="40" xml:id="d303-f1-content">
                <p>The Conference had been postponed from October 1927.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d303-f2" n="42" xml:id="d303-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
